    "directions": [
      "Mix 170 g of flour with 85 g of sugar in a food processor. Add 85 g of butter (cut into small cubes) from the fridge and blend well. Add 2 tablespoons of milk and blend again to obtain coarse sand.",
      "Dump the mixture into a 28 cm pie dish and press/pack the dough with your fingers to line the dish.",
      "Scale down the recipe to use 120 g of flour, 60 g of sugar, and 60 g of butter. Replace a heaping tablespoon of flour with unsweetened cocoa powder.",
      "Line 3 tartlets with the dough, place circles of parchment paper and ceramic baking weights on them, and bake at 200°C (400°F) for 10 minutes.",
      "Cool the tartlets on a rack.",
      "Melt 40 g of Valrhona baking chocolate in the microwave and brush it onto the tartlet shells. Place them in the fridge to cool.",
      "Melt 50 g of sugar in a non-stick saucepan until completely caramelized. Add 1 teaspoon of unsweetened cocoa and mix thoroughly.",
      "Pour the caramel onto a silicon baking sheet and draw shapes quickly while it's still hot and liquid.",
      "Heat 100 ml of crème fleurette until the first teeny bubble appears. Pour it over 150 g of broken chocolate pieces and mix thoroughly with a fork.",
      "Add 2 egg yolks and 40 g of butter, ensuring no lumps remain. Mix to create a thick chocolate cream.",
      "Pour the ganache into the tartlet shells. Add one caramel shape to each tartlet.",
      "Place the tartlets in the fridge for the ganache to set."
    ],
